### Cross-phase whole-system checkpoint gate

Every transition to a later roadmap phase is blocked on one whole-system
checkpoint. This is an architecture and model-delta adjudication, not a test
summary and not a review of only the latest diff. It applies after the selected
V1 mutation scope, after deterministic smoke and the complete V1 rerun, before
constructive simplification, after the simplification environment freeze and
every accepted cleanup slice, and before release reconciliation, performance
acceptance and the final production review.

Each checkpoint must regenerate its derivable inputs from the exact Git tree
and the existing machine authorities. Cargo features and the Rust module graph
own source roles; `architecture-contract.json` and `review-behaviors.json` own
semantic and evidence bindings; test discovery, source symbols, selectors,
counts, coverage, commands and Git deltas must be generated and checked. Manual
path lists, copied test names, hand-curated mutation selectors, sampled counts
and prose-only coverage claims are forbidden. Human judgment is reserved for
business/attack provenance, semantic equivalence and topology choice; it
cannot replace a mechanically discoverable fact.

The checkpoint must review the complete trusted boundary and state basis,
single-authority and linear-capability conservation, transition totality,
resource/effect ownership, task/lock/wait-for/publication graphs, preserved
parallel work and canonical ordering, external observations and compatibility,
and fixed plus adversarial cost bounds. It must compare the complete current
architecture with the frozen baseline-to-target ledger, classify each risk as
eliminated, mitigated or transferred, and give every residual an owner,
falsifier and explicit defer decision. Duplicate authority or policy,
invariant growth, new failure domains, concurrency loss, compatibility drift
and snowball complexity are phase blockers rather than cleanup debt.

Where a claim is a state machine, set relation, conservation law, equivalence,
partial order, finite rank or complexity bound, its authority is executable
mathematics: sealed Rust types and constructors, the pure reference model with
property/differential tests, deterministic schedule checking, and TLC or a
more specialized checker only for a named residual claim. Manual inspection
and prose may explain a trusted boundary or decision but cannot discharge the
claim. If implementation reveals a new semantic case, authority, failure
domain, topology or compatibility boundary, production work stops until the
model and fixed plan are updated and re-adjudicated. The durable checkpoint
records the exact revision, generated inputs, model/plan delta, residuals and
next action; no later phase inherits a pass implicitly.

